 Growth & Marketing Analytics – Campaign & Channel Performance

This project analyzes marketing performance across multiple paid and organic acquisition channels for a FinTech product.
It uses a synthetic dataset of 50,000 users and multiple campaigns, simulating a real Growth/Marketing analytics workflow — evaluating channel efficiency, ROI, LTV and CAC, and providing actionable insights.

Dataset Overview
Campaign-Level Data (df_campaigns)

Each row represents a marketing campaign with:
Spend
Impressions
Clicks
Installs
Signups
Deposits
Revenue
CTR (Click Through Rate)
CPC (Cost Per Click)
CPA (Cost Per Signup)
Conversion Rates
ROAS (Return On Ad Spend)


User-Level Data (df_users)
Each row represents a user acquired through a specific channel:
Acquisition date
Channel (Facebook / Google / TikTok / YouTube / Influencers / Organic)
Campaign name
Country
Device type
Signup / Deposit actions
Transaction count
LTV (lifetime value)
30-day retention
The dataset is designed to mimic real-world behavior and CAC/LTV differences between channels.

Key Visualizations :

ROAS by Channel
TikTok dominates performance with extremely high ROAS (~65).
Facebook and Influencers also strong; Google underperforms.

CPA (Cost per Signup) by Channel
Google is the most expensive channel (~3.45).
Facebook, TikTok, YouTube and Influencers show much lower CPA.

Average LTV by Channel
Organic and Influencers produce the highest-value users (~84–85).
TikTok users have lower LTV but extremely high ROAS.


Growth Insights

TikTok provides the strongest ROI – extremely high ROAS, relatively low CPA.
Google is expensive and inefficient – highest CPA, lowest ROAS.
Facebook balances cost and return – strong ROAS and low CPA.
Influencers deliver high-quality users – high LTV and solid ROAS.
Organic users are the most valuable group – highest LTV, infinite ROAS (zero spend).

Recommendation: Reallocate budget from Google → TikTok, Facebook, Influencers and invest in SEO/referrals to boost the high-value Organic segment.

Summary

This project simulates a full Growth Analytics workflow — measuring marketing effectiveness, diagnosing waste, optimizing spend, and recommending high-impact actions using data.
